# IT Asset Management System

!!!!!!!!!!!!DISCLAIMER!!!!!!!!!!!!!
!!FOR EDUCATIONAL PURPOSES ONLY; NOT SUCURED WITH LIVE USE IN MIND!!

A Java-based IT asset management application developed as part of my university studies.

The application provides a graphical interface for managing hardware, software and employee records, while also incorporating system information collection and vulnerability information from the NIST National Vulnerability Database (NVD).

## Overview

The purpose of this project was to develop an application capable of helping an organisation maintain an inventory of its IT assets and associate software vulnerabilities with those assets.

The application combines:

- Java application development
- JavaFX graphical user interface
- MySQL database management
- Hardware and software inventory
- User authentication and access control
- Windows system information collection
- NIST NVD vulnerability lookup

## Features

### Asset Management

The application allows users to manage information relating to:

- Hardware
- Software
- Employees
- Asset assignments
- Software installed on devices

Users can create, view, update and delete records through the graphical interface.

### Hardware Management

Hardware records can contain information such as:

- Device name
- Serial number
- Manufacturer
- Model
- Operating system
- Assigned employee

### Software Management

Software can be recorded against assets and managed through the application.

The application can also retrieve vulnerability information relating to software through the NIST National Vulnerability Database API.

### Vulnerability Information

The system integrates with the **NIST National Vulnerability Database (NVD)** to retrieve information about known software vulnerabilities.

This allows vulnerability information to be associated with software recorded within the asset-management system.

The application can display information such as:

- CVE identifiers
- Vulnerability descriptions
- Severity information
- CVSS information
- Published vulnerability information

### System Information Collection

The project also includes functionality for collecting information from a Windows system, including hardware and software information.

This was intended to demonstrate how an asset-management system could automate parts of the asset discovery process rather than relying entirely on manual data entry.

### User Authentication

The application includes a login system with different levels of access.

This demonstrates the use of authentication and access-control concepts within the application.

## Technologies

| Technology | Purpose |
| Java | Application development |
| JavaFX | Graphical user interface |
| MySQL | Database management |
| JDBC | Database connectivity |
| NIST NVD API | Vulnerability information |
| Windows system commands | Hardware/software information collection |

